[john.russell@canrem.UUCP (John Russell) writes:]
[] A rethink of the whole spell system would make the game more balanced.

[hairston@henry.ece.cmu.edu (David Hairston) writes:]
[] personally, i would do the following ...
[] 5) introduce a timeout to spell-casting and also remember the level ...
[] ...
[]    the timeout would be non-wizard: 120 * n and for wizards: 80 * n.

hmm, this need amending.  you should be able to use a level 1 spell
over and over without a timeout so the formulae should read:
non-wizard: 120 * (n - 1) and for wizards 80 * (n - 1).  also,
during the timeout there should be no penalty for attempting to
use a spell whose level is too high (except that you can't cast it)
and you should get a feeling about this, perhaps: "You currently
feel magically inept".  finally, when the timeout is over you should
get a feeling to the effect that: "You feel magically better".

btw, the Oracle would know about certain rules/laws concerning
spells ...

and the Oracle wouldn't give random advice, rather offer to give
advice on the subject of your choosing from a selection of topics.
naturally there would be more topics and there would be topics of
use/interest in the current game as opposed to simply a list of
archived facts ... ;)

